{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: We have two RNA-only single-profile experiments showing that a learned nonlinear encoder (scvi_n200, 0.520 acc) modestly beats a linear one (PCA-2000, 0.485 acc). However, the image modality is entirely unexplored—we have zero data on whether image features carry independent predictive signal. This is the largest source of uncertainty in the design space, as it determines whether the 36 multimodal configurations (configs 016-051) are worth pursuing at all. 2) What this tests: config_010 (image-only, single profile, ResNet-50) establishes the performance floor for the image modality in direct analogy to how config_001 established the RNA floor. It isolates the image encoder's contribution with no confounding from RNA, aggregation, or fusion. 3) Why it is the best next experiment: Before investing limited budget in complex multimodal fusion or multiprofile aggregation, we need to know whether the image signal is strong enough to be worth combining. If image-only performs competitively (≥0.50), multimodal fusion becomes a high-priority direction; if it is weak (<0.45), we should focus remaining budget on RNA improvements (multiprofile, scgpt encoder). This single experiment gates the entire multimodal branch of the search and is the highest-information, lowest-confounding next step."
}

